    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required de-duplicating the computed `customerCode` on collision by appending `-<n>` (smallest `n` \u2265 2).\n\nI updated `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.service` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`):\n\n- Injected the existing `OwnerRepository` bean (same pattern as sibling functions like `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`).\n- After computing the base `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, it gathers all existing owners' `customerCode`s and, if the base is already taken, appends `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 choosing the smallest `n \u2265 2` that is unique.\n- Updated the class Javadoc to document the de-duplication rule.\n\nResult: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. The acceptance test `coreCustomerCodesStayUnique` (distinct owners get distinct codes) passes, and it's the only test class in the project.",
